---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="SMS Consent Evidence — Foremann"
  description="How Foremann captures end-user consent before any SMS is sent through a contractor's business number."
>
  <Nav />

  <section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">A2P 10DLC Compliance</div>
      <h1 class="display">SMS Consent Evidence</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This page documents how Foremann captures end-user consent before any
        SMS is sent through a contractor's dedicated business number. It is
        intended as evidence for carriers, The Campaign Registry (TCR), and
        any compliance reviewer auditing our A2P 10DLC campaign.
      </p>
      <div class="legal-meta">Last updated: May 5, 2026</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-body">
    <div class="wrap legal-doc">

      <h2>What Foremann is</h2>
      <p>
        Foremann is a B2B SaaS product that provisions a dedicated business
        phone number for independent trade businesses (plumbers, electricians,
        HVAC technicians, landscapers). Each contractor operates their own
        number and uses it to communicate one-to-one with their own existing
        customers and leads. Messages are conversational and contractor-initiated,
        not automated bulk sends, marketing, or promotional traffic.
      </p>

      <h2>How consent is captured</h2>
      <p>
        Foremann supports two opt-in paths. Both produce a verifiable record
        before any outbound SMS is sent.
      </p>

      <h3>Path 1 — Inbound-first (customer texts first)</h3>
      <p>
        The trade business publishes their Foremann number on invoices,
        business cards, signage, vehicle wraps, and their website. When a
        homeowner texts that number first, the inbound message itself
        establishes consent for the contractor to reply. No additional
        opt-in step is required.
      </p>

      <h3>Path 2 — In-app consent attestation (manual contact add)</h3>
      <p>
        When a contractor manually adds a contact inside the Foremann app —
        typically after meeting the customer in person, on a service call,
        or by phone — the app requires the contractor to check an
        attestation box (unchecked by default) that reads:
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>"I confirm this contact has agreed to receive text messages from my business."</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        The "Save Client" action is blocked until the box is checked. When
        the contact is created, Foremann records:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The timestamp of the attestation (<code>sms_consent_given_at</code>)</li>
        <li>The user who attested (<code>sms_consent_given_by_user_id</code>)</li>
        <li>The source of the consent record (<code>sms_consent_source = 'manual_add_attestation'</code>)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This record is retained for the life of the contact and is
        available for audit on request.
      </p>

      <h2>Screenshot of the consent gate</h2>
      <p>
        The screenshot below shows the consent attestation as it appears in
        the Foremann mobile app when a contractor manually adds a new contact.
      </p>
      <figure class="evidence-figure">
        <img
          src="/consent-evidence-screenshot.png"
          alt="Foremann mobile app — Add Client screen with required SMS consent attestation checkbox reading 'I confirm this contact has agreed to receive text messages from my business.'"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Foremann mobile app — Add Client screen. The consent attestation
          checkbox is required and unchecked by default.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>Opt-out handling</h2>
      <p>
        Recipients can reply <code>STOP</code>, <code>STOPALL</code>,
        <code>UNSUBSCRIBE</code>, <code>CANCEL</code>, <code>END</code>,
        <code>QUIT</code>, <code>REVOKE</code>, <code>OPTOUT</code>, or
        <code>OPT-OUT</code> at any time. Foremann sends a confirmation
        ("You're unsubscribed and won't get more texts. Reply START to opt back in.")
        and blocks all further outbound messages from that business number to
        that recipient at the platform level. Individual contractors cannot
        bypass or disable opt-out handling. <code>HELP</code> returns:
        "Reply STOP to unsubscribe. Msg &amp; data rates may apply."
        <code>START</code> re-subscribes.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclosures on first message</h2>
      <p>
        The first outbound message Foremann sends to a new recipient from a
        contractor's number includes the disclosure
        "Reply STOP to opt out." Subsequent conversational messages do not
        repeat the disclosure, consistent with CTIA Messaging Principles &amp;
        Best Practices for ongoing 1:1 business communication.
      </p>

      <h2>Data handling</h2>
      <p>
        Mobile phone numbers and SMS-related personal information are not
        shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional
        purposes. Full details are in our
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For compliance, audit, or carrier review questions, email
        <a href="mailto:compliance@foremann.app">compliance@foremann.app</a>.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-hero {
    padding: clamp(60px, 8vw, 100px) 0 clamp(30px, 4vw, 50px);
  }
  .legal-hero .display {
    font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 80px);
    margin: 18px 0 20px;
  }
  .legal-hero .lede { max-width: 720px; }
  .legal-meta {
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .legal-body {
    padding: clamp(30px, 5vw, 60px) 0 clamp(60px, 9vw, 120px);
  }
  .legal-doc {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .legal-doc h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    font-size: 26px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
  }
  .legal-doc h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal-doc h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 28px 0 8px;
  }
  .legal-doc p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .legal-doc ul {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .legal-doc li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .legal-doc strong { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 700; }
  .legal-doc a {
    color: var(--rust);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .legal-doc a:hover { color: var(--rust-dark); }
  .legal-doc code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--sand);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .evidence-figure {
    margin: 24px 0 32px;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .evidence-figure img {
    display: block;
    max-width: 360px;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    background: var(--sand);
  }
  .evidence-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
